<%# Figma frame 06. Devise has no screen here — `create` redirects to the
    sign-in form with a flash, which is a page the user has no reason to read.

    No form fields: the address is already known, it came in with the redirect.
    The only action is resending to that same address, so it is a POST back to
    the same endpoint rather than a link, and the address rides in a hidden
    field instead of the URL — a reset email in a query string ends up in logs
    and in the Referer of anything the page links to.

    Copy is the designer's apart from the body, which that frame's export did
    not include. %>
<div class="auth-card">
  <div class="auth-badge auth-badge--info">
    <%= render "shared/auth_icon", name: :mail, size: 28 %>
  </div>

  <h1 class="auth-card__title">Check your email</h1>
  <%# Neutral about whether it matched, because the endpoint is: see
      User.send_reset_password_instructions. Says "matches" rather than naming
      it an email address — the mobile apps send `login`, which may be a
      username. %>
  <p class="auth-card__subtitle">
    If <strong><%= @reset_email %></strong> matches an AirCasting account, a link
    to reset the password is on its way. It stays valid for 6 hours.
  </p>

  <%= form_tag password_path(resource_name), method: :post, class: "auth-form" do %>
    <%= hidden_field_tag "user[login]", @reset_email %>
    <%= submit_tag "Send it again", class: "auth-button" %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "devise/shared/links" %>
</div>
